 exited agent get `agent has exited`. Only the configured group and the operator
 ids from setup are accepted; everything else is dropped and logged.
 
+For queued Codex questions (the screen says `shift+← to answer`), send
+`/keys shift+left`, then `/screen`. Use `/keys up` or `/keys down` to
+select an answer and `/keys enter` to confirm it. These raw keys also work
+while Codex reports working; a plain digit in that state would be a new prompt.
+
+`/git diff remote` shows the local side since the merge base with the current
+branch's upstream: unpushed commits, staged and unstaged edits, and untracked
+files that Git does not ignore. It uses the tracking reference from the last
+`git fetch`, does not fetch or modify the real index, and does not enter nested
+repositories or submodules. With detached HEAD (including colocated Jujutsu
+repositories), it uses the configured `origin/HEAD` instead of an upstream.
+An unavailable comparison base returns a setup hint.
+Large patches arrive as files under the same 5 MB output limit as other diffs.
+
 ## Claude Code commands
 
 The four Claude Code commands are typed verbatim through `agent.prompt`, so
